<title>NETHERLANDS: EMU convergence to use 1998 budgets - de Silguy.</title>
<headline>EMU convergence to use 1998 budgets - de Silguy.</headline>
<dateline>NOORDWIJK, Netherlands 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Affairs Commissioner Yves Thibault de Silguy said on Friday that member states' 1998 budgets would be used to set sustainable EMU convergence.</p>
<p>&quot;We will take into account effectively 1998 budgets in order to ensure that 1997 deficits will not have been reduced by one-off measures,&quot; de Silguy told a news briefing ahead of a two-day informal meeting of European Union finance ministers in the Dutch coastal resort of Noordwijk.</p>
</text>
